# Branch Naming and Pull Request Guidelines

## Branch Naming Convention

**Format:** `<user-prefix>/[<task-id>-]<very-short-hyphenated-description>`

Task IDs are optional. Use one of these formats:
- With task ID: `<user-prefix>/<task-id>-<description>`
- Without task ID: `<user-prefix>/<description>`

### Examples:
- `cmiller/12345-forms-validation-fix` (with Trello card ID)
- `cmiller/add-new-form-field` (without task ID)
- `cmiller/update-form-wizard` (without task ID)

### Guidelines:
- Use your username/initials as prefix
- Include Trello card ID if available (optional)
- Keep description short and hyphenated
- Be descriptive but concise
- Use lowercase letters and hyphens only

## Pull Request Title Format

**Format:** `[<task-id>: ]<brief-description>`

Task IDs are optional. Use one of these formats:
- With task ID: `<task-id>: <brief-description>`
- Without task ID: `<brief-description>`

### Examples:
- `12345: Fix form validation errors` (with Trello card ID)
- `Add new date picker field type` (without task ID)
- `Update form wizard navigation` (without task ID)

### Guidelines:
- Start with Trello card ID if available (optional)
- Follow with a colon and space if using task ID
- Use present tense, imperative mood
- Keep under 60 characters when possible
- Be specific about what the PR accomplishes

## Pull Request Description Format

**Required structure for all pull requests:**

1. **Description of changes** at the top
2. **Task/ticket link** (if using project management tool)
3. **No file lists** - changed files are already obvious from the diff
4. **Keep descriptions concise** and focused on what was changed and why

### Example PR Description:
```
## Summary
Added form validation for email fields. Users will now see clear error messages when entering invalid email addresses.

## Related
[Trello Card](https://trello.com/c/card-id)
```

**Note:** Include Trello card link if the PR is related to a specific card. If no card exists, omit the "Related" section.

## PR Creation Commands

**Use this streamlined command for creating PRs:**

With Trello card:
```bash
gh pr create --title "<task-id>: <brief-description>" --body "## Summary
<description of changes>

## Related
[Trello Card](<trello-card-url>)" --base main
```

Without Trello card:
```bash
gh pr create --title "<brief-description>" --body "## Summary
<description of changes>" --base main
```

## Quality Checklist

**Before creating PRs:**
- [ ] Branch name follows convention
- [ ] PR title includes task ID (if applicable)
- [ ] Description explains what and why
- [ ] Task/ticket is linked (if applicable)
- [ ] No file lists in description
- [ ] Changes are focused and atomic
- [ ] Tests pass (if applicable)
- [ ] Code is linted and formatted

## Commit and PR Message Guidelines

**❌ AVOID EMOJIS in commits and pull requests:**
- **No emojis in commit messages** - Keep them professional and clear
- **No emojis in PR titles or descriptions** - Use plain text for better readability
- **Focus on clear, descriptive language** instead of visual symbols

**Examples of what to avoid:**
- ❌ `🚀 Add new feature`
- ❌ `🐛 Fix bug in forms`
- ❌ `✨ Update UI components`

**Examples of preferred format:**
- ✅ `Add new feature for form validation`
- ✅ `Fix bug in form submission flow`
- ✅ `Update UI components for better accessibility`

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

❌ **Don't include:**
- Lists of changed files
- Emojis in titles or descriptions
- Vague descriptions like "fix stuff"
- Multiple unrelated changes in one PR

✅ **Do include:**
- Clear explanation of changes
- Task/ticket link (if applicable)
- Focused, single-purpose changes
- Professional, descriptive language
